{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/vn/reviews/id107364950"}, "name":{"label":"maggiekieu"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2023-11-08T01:10:59-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"1"}, "im:version":{"label":"7.88.2"}, "id":{"label":"10562545547"}, "title":{"label":"TIME WASTING & IRRESPONSIBLE CUSTOMER SERVICES"}, "content":{"label":"I’ve been using the app for years, with adding all of my Frequency Card information there, choose it every time I book my flights. Then after all, when we check on the Airline Mileage information, it’s not recognize AT ALL. And you contact the Customer Services with asking many questions, then their answer is: “There is no way for us to check the mileage points for the past bookings/flights. I suggest you to contact the airline directly for further assistance” ??? How can an action mistakenly happen on Trip.com app leads the users to reach to the Airline to figure out how and why it not working as expected? Then why you have that function on the app? having trust from loyalty users, and of course if its upcoming flights the mileage is not available or you’re only aware that its not linking after the flight is taken and mileage closing report ready. 1. Improve your Frequency Card working process 2. Improve your Online Customer Services or provide more actionable and reasonable solution to customers instead of kicking the ball to the airlines like that. Then they asked for more information, and promise with revert in 24hrs, and in the next email, they repeat the exact same things.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/vn/review?id=681752345&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"2"}}], "updated":{"label":"2026-10-25T12:33:37-07:00"}, "rights":{"label":"Copyright 2008 Apple Inc."}, "title":{"label":"iTunes Store: Customer Reviews"}, "icon":{"l